<section id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-kicker">What she does</p>
    <h2 class="sec-title">Everything the room needs, without a public listing.</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead">These are the features that actually ship in L5 today — from the bot itself and the official guide. Nothing here is a promise of a public bot or of numbers we don’t publish.</p>
    <div class="grid3">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 10h.01M12 10h.01M16 10h.01M21 12c0 4.4-4 8-9 8l-4 2v-3.1A8.2 8.2 0 0 1 3 12c0-4.4 4-8 9-8s9 3.6 9 8z"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Chat, in character</h3>
        <p>Mention her or DM her and she answers. Moods — Default, Chill, Chaotic, Sleepy, Hype, or Sassy — change how she talks. In the panel, a live feed lets you reply as L5.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M7 8h10M7 12h6"/></svg></div>
        <h3>A keyed control room</h3>
        <p>Status, features, scheduled posts, and logs live in a signed-in dashboard. You get in with a key Julian issues, or by requesting one from the sign-in page.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Events &amp; reminders</h3>
        <p>Mods can type <span class="k">!event 10/31 7pm …</span> or “remind everyone friday 7pm…”. She posts at that time and can ping an opt-in Events role. Anyone can list them with <span class="k">!events</span>.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 18v-7l7-4 7 4v7"/><path d="M9 18v-5h6v5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Go-live posts</h3>
        <p>When a configured Twitch stream starts, she posts once in the channel you pick and pings people who opted in. A drop and reconnect does not send a second announcement.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8.5-8 9-4.5-.5-8-4-8-9V7l8-4z"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Spam cleanup &amp; shield</h3>
        <p>She deletes obvious fake Nitro/Steam gift links, unauthorized @everyone-with-a-link, and the same message blasted across channels, then times the sender out. A separate anti-raid shield watches for mass bans, channel deletes, and bot raids.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 9h8M8 13h5"/><path d="M4 6h16v12H8l-4 3V6z"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Room tools</h3>
        <p>Custom command triggers, reaction roles, welcome messages, and scheduled or repeating posts — all from the Features tab in the control room.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

