<section>
  <div class="wrap split reverse">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="sec-kicker">In the server</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title">She answers, reminds, and keeps the floor clear.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead" style="margin-bottom:0">Talk to her in a channel or a DM. Schedule a stream night in plain language. If someone posts the usual fake-gift scam, she handles it and writes it down in the mod log — without touching admins or mods.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="visual">
      <div class="mock">
        <div class="bubble"><small>in the server</small>remind everyone friday 7pm stream</div>
        <div class="bubble me"><small>L5</small>ok, I’ll post it Friday at 7pm Central and ping Event pings. Cancel with <span class="k">!cancelevent</span>.</div>
        <div class="ev"><div class="d">Fri<b>7pm</b></div><div><b>stream</b><div style="color:var(--mut)">Posted to the events channel · opt-in ping</div></div></div>
        <div class="log"><b>Cleanup (example)</b> — fake gift link removed, sender timed out 10 minutes. Admins and mods are never touched.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="commands">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-kicker">Commands</p>
    <h2 class="sec-title">The prefix is <em style="font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:400">!</em> — plus a couple of slash commands.</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead">This list is taken from L5’s own <span class="k">!help</span> and the official guide. Custom triggers you add in the panel show up at the bottom of <span class="k">!help</span> on that server.</p>
    <div class="cmds">
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!help</span><p>Lists built-in commands, plus any custom ones on that server.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!roll 2d6</span><p>Dice. Default is 1d6; up to 20 dice.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!coin</span><p>Heads or tails.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!8ball</span><p>A classic magic-8-ball reply.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!pick a, b, c</span><p>Chooses one option.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!poll q | a | b</span><p>Posts a poll with reactions. A question alone gets thumbs up/down.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!remind 10m text</span><p>Pings you later (s/m/h/d, up to 7 days).</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!avatar @user</span><p>Shows that user’s avatar, or yours.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!userinfo @user</span><p>Join date and roles.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!serverinfo</span><p>Member, channel, and role counts.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!purge 10</span><p>Deletes recent messages. <span class="who">Mods only (Manage Messages)</span></p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!events</span><p>Lists upcoming events. <span class="who">Anyone</span></p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!event 10/31 7pm …</span><p>Schedules a post. “remind everyone friday 7pm…” also works. <span class="who">Mods only</span></p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!cancelevent code</span><p>Cancels one, using the code L5 gave you. <span class="who">Mods only</span></p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!requestlogin</span><p>Asks Julian for a panel key. Also available as <span class="k">/requestlogin</span>.</p></div>
      <div class="cmd"><span class="k">!l5help</span><p>DMs you the panel and guide links. Also <span class="k">!panel</span> and <span class="k">!guide</span>.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cmd-note"><span class="k">/privacy</span> is a short, in-Discord note on how L5 treats chats.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="start">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-kicker">Getting started</p>
    <h2 class="sec-title">Three steps. No public invite button.</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <b>01</b>
        <h3>Ask for a key</h3>
        <p>If she is already in a server you share, type <span class="k">!requestlogin</span>. Otherwise open Request access on the sign-in page and include your Discord user ID.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <b>02</b>
        <h3>Wait for the DM</h3>
        <p>Julian reviews the request. If he approves it, the panel key is sent in a Discord DM. It is never shown in the browser.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <b>03</b>
        <h3>Sign in</h3>
        <p>Open the control room and sign in, or type <span class="k">!help</span> in a server she is in. The <a href="https://l5.memegames.net/guide">guide</a> walks through the panel in plain language.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

